  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue is clear: all 7 items are closed, including one that arrived while I was working. Everything was done under refill protocol RBC-RX-05. New results and corrections came in partway through, and they changed two decisions: two lisinopril refills are now on hold waiting for your review.\n\n**Needs your review today (2 urgent tasks assigned to you)**\n- **Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg:** I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill. His August outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count; his last valid potassium was 4.5 (Jan 2026). I also ordered a repeat BMP. Then a new St. Brigid pre-op BMP (drawn 10/20, good sample) showed potassium 5.8. I put the refill on hold (mr-t0001) and created your review task (task-t0019). I sent him a corrected message telling him not to fill it, which also lists warning symptoms. His repeat BMP order (sr-t0002) is still open for you to use or cancel. His hernia repair is now 11/12.\n- **Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg (raised from 10 mg on 9/18):** I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill: potassium 5.2, creatinine up 23.6%. Today the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is a 35.5% rise within 4 weeks of the dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I put the refill on hold (mr-t0005), created your review task (task-t0020) and sent him a corrected message.\n\n**Completed refills**\n- **Samuel Price, metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. His corrected eGFR is 58, and his HbA1c was 7.1% on 8/19 (outside lab report). He and the pharmacy asked three times in total; I placed one order and closed all three messages.\n- **Marcus Webb (pt-0031), metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. His eGFR 39 from 10/14 was marked entered in error (mislabelled sample), so I didn't use it; his valid eGFR is 92. HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28.\n- **Marcus Webb, lisinopril 10 mg:** his last BMP was over 12 months old, so I first gave a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP. A valid BMP drawn 10/22 then came in (potassium 4.6, eGFR 90), so I replaced it with a 90-day supply and 1 refill (mr-t0021). The BMP order I placed (sr-t0012) is no longer needed for this refill. I couldn't cancel it with my tools, so you may want to cancel it.\n\n**Messages and records**\n- Each patient got a reply, and a corrected or updated message once a decision changed.\n- Each chart has a note explaining the decisions and corrections.\n- I closed the three new results for these patients from your results queue. The other 8 results in that queue (other patients, including critical potassiums for pt-0016 and pt-0008) were outside this task and are untouched.",
